---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { AUTHOR, SITE } from "../lib/site.mjs";
---

<Base
  title="Author"
  description="Colin Dixon — author of The Ministry of Doubt. Physics, mathematics and IT background; Australian technologist and builder of electiontracker.au."
>
  <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
    <header class="hero author-hero">
      <div class="author-hero__text">
        <p class="eyebrow">Author</p>
        <h1>{AUTHOR.name}</h1>
        <p class="lede">{AUTHOR.shortBio}</p>
        <p class="pill">Based in {AUTHOR.location}</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="author-portrait">
        <img
          src={AUTHOR.photo}
          alt={AUTHOR.photoAlt}
          width="1024"
          height="1024"
          decoding="async"
          fetchpriority="high"
        />
      </figure>
    </header>

    <h2>Approach</h2>
    <p>
      The narrator of <em>{SITE.name}</em> comes from physics, mathematics and information technology —
      models, assumptions, probability, systems and falsifiability — not from a career in punditry.
      The voice aims to be calm, dry and unimpressed by pomposity from either establishment institutions
      or conspiracy culture.
    </p>
    <p>
      Influences in quality rather than imitation: investigative technical storytelling, first-principles
      honesty about self-deception, the psychology of belief, and a stubborn insistence that objective
      reality is not optional.
    </p>

    <h2>Public work</h2>
    <p>
      Colin publishes independent, sourced public-interest tools. The flagship example is the
      <a href={AUTHOR.electionTracker}>Australian Election Tracker</a> — a candidacy and polling ledger
      where material claims carry dated public sources, open data exports and a written methodology.
      That same evidence discipline is the design north star for the Ministry of Doubt companion tracker.
    </p>

    <ul class="meta-list">
      <li>
        <span>Book</span>
        <span><a href="/book">{SITE.name}</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>Election data</span>
        <span><a href={AUTHOR.electionTracker}>electiontracker.au</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>Profile</span>
        <span><a href={AUTHOR.ozol}>ozol.com</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>Publisher</span>
        <span><a href={AUTHOR.oze}>OZE</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>X</span>
        <span><a href={AUTHOR.x}>{AUTHOR.xHandle}</a></span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span>LinkedIn</span>
        <span><a href={AUTHOR.linkedin}>colindixon</a></span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      This page is a public author bio for the book project. It is not a dump of private research notes,
      draft chapters or case dossiers.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
